WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.469 --> 00:00:06.180
Two guys are sitting together in a bar
in the remote Alaskan wilderness arguing

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:10.830
about the existence of God. While they're
old friends they have very different

00:00:10.830 --> 00:00:19.140
ideas on God: one is a priest and the
other is an atheist. The atheist says

00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:25.230
"Look it's not like I haven't given God a
chance, I've even tried the prayer thing.

00:00:25.230 --> 00:00:32.610
It didn't work!" The priest asks with some
incredulity: "Did you really pray? When did

00:00:32.610 --> 00:00:38.250
this happen?"
"Just last month" replies the atheist "I

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:43.110
got caught away from the camp and a
terrible blizzard I was totally lost and

00:00:43.110 --> 00:00:49.500
I couldn't see a thing it was 20 degrees
below zero and so I prayed I fell to my

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:55.289
knees in the snow and cried out: Oh God
if there is a god I'm lost in this

00:00:55.289 --> 00:01:01.980
blizzard and I'm going to die if you
don't help me!" the priest looks at the

00:01:01.980 --> 00:01:08.790
atheist puzzled and says: "Well, then you
must believe in God now, after all here

00:01:08.790 --> 00:01:15.479
you are, alive!" The atheist rolls his eyes
and replies: "No, no that's not how it

00:01:15.479 --> 00:01:20.009
happened! A couple of Eskimos came
wandering by and showed me the way back

00:01:20.009 --> 00:01:29.790
to the camp". So, where do such different
perspectives come from? Confirmation bias

00:01:29.790 --> 00:01:36.060
is a tendency to look for, interpret and
recall information in ways that affirm

00:01:36.060 --> 00:01:41.880
our preconception. Whenever we encounter
objective facts on an issue we look at

00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:46.829
them through the lens of our own beliefs.
As a result we see and overrate where

00:01:46.829 --> 00:01:52.829
the to intercept. The bias is strongest
for emotionally charged issues or when

00:01:52.829 --> 00:01:58.049
we search for desired outcomes.

00:01:58.060 --> 00:02:03.370
Wrapped inside popular narratives,
cultural beliefs and family values a

00:02:03.370 --> 00:02:10.490
confirmation bias often gets passed on
for generations. The priest learned from

00:02:10.490 --> 00:02:15.710
his ancestors that God is behind
everything. The atheist was raised within

00:02:15.710 --> 00:02:21.290
a family that believed only in
scientific knowledge. When we are

00:02:21.290 --> 00:02:26.300
confronted with unfamiliar or new
situations a bias helps us to draw

00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:31.730
fast conclusions. If every encounter with
a stranger would require us to think of

00:02:31.730 --> 00:02:37.460
all sorts of possible outcomes, we would
not come to any conclusions. Economically

00:02:37.460 --> 00:02:45.410
speaking it would be too costly. To
survive in a dangerous world we learn to

00:02:45.410 --> 00:02:50.180
operate like storytelling,
pattern-seeking animals, each one of us

00:02:50.180 --> 00:02:56.540
thinking that our story and our head is
the right one. Today we can afford to

00:02:56.540 --> 00:03:01.970
slow down and think more deeply about
certain issues. When we do this we can

00:03:01.970 --> 00:03:07.700
become aware of our own biases. We begin
to realize that things are often more

00:03:07.700 --> 00:03:10.900
complicated than we thought.

00:03:11.170 --> 00:03:17.090
Psychologist Peter Cathcart Wason who
coined the term confirmation bias left

00:03:17.090 --> 00:03:22.400
us with this fun little hypothesis rule
discovery task, let's see if you can do

00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:30.910
it? What's the rule behind the sequence
of numbers: 2 4 6 ? And what comes next?

00:03:30.910 --> 00:03:35.780
Write the correct number and the rule we
are looking for in the comments below!

00:03:35.780 --> 00:03:43.689
Now, fast!

00:03:43.689 --> 00:03:49.040
Psychologists and nobel prize winner
Daniel Kahneman said: "A reliable way to

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:54.140
make people believe in falsehoods is
frequent repetition. Because familiarity

00:03:54.140 --> 00:04:00.370
is not easily distinguished from truth.".
Which means if there is time to reflect

00:04:00.370 --> 00:04:08.449
slowing down is likely to be a good idea!

